Package: innova2-app
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: innova2-areg-dkms
Suggests: mstflint, python3-numpy
Description: management app and shell health tool for the Mellanox Innova-2 Flex card
 innova2_app does what Mellanox's innova2_flex_app 18.07.00 did, with the
 same menus and options: query and select the FPGA image, grant JTAG access,
 read identity, temperature, fan and power, run the DDR and PCI tests, and
 burn a User image into flash. It works on current kernels and
 MLNX_OFED/DOCA-OFED releases, which no longer ship mlx5_fpga_tools.
 .
 Image select and the JTAG grant need the innova2-areg-dkms kernel module
 (or the vendor mlx5_fpga_tools module from MLNX_OFED 5.2). Without it, the
 card can still be queried through MFT's mlxreg or mstflint's mstreg.
 .
 innova2-smi queries and tests the Innova-2 XRT shell (fp8c lineage): card
 discovery from the ConnectX-5, shell identity, DDR/ECC, clocks, every
 temperature source, the thermal throttle, PCIe, PR, P2P and the flight
 recorder; a passive concerns-only check for cron; and active tests (validate,
 DDR soak, throttle tier walk, PR stress, flash read-back). Its active tests
 need XRT (and python3-numpy for the DDR soak).

Package: innova2-areg-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers
Description: innova2_areg kernel module (DKMS) for the Innova-2 Flex card
 Re-creates the /dev/<bdf>_mlx5_fpga_tools device node, with the vendor's
 ioctls, on top of the kernel's exported mlx5_core_access_reg(). This is what
 innova2_app needs for image select and the JTAG grant on kernels and OFED
 releases without the vendor mlx5_fpga_tools module (MLNX_OFED 5.3 and later).
 .
 DKMS rebuilds the module on every kernel or OFED update, and it is loaded at
 boot. Do not install it on a host that still has the vendor module.
